{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T065630Z_dev-05_flat_2033", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper does not quote a detection significance (σ or TS) for the GCE in its 17.7-year analysis. It only says the fitted GCE flux is nonzero in all 80 diffuse-emission models, and that \"this observation alone does not establish its statistical significance\". It also says the Δ(-2lnL) differences between the non-nested diffuse models cannot be read as squared Gaussian significances. The fit statistics it reports are χ² values for dark matter spectral fits (e.g. χ²_min = 27.50 for 12 dof in the b b̄ channel), which measure goodness of fit and not the significance of the excess.", "found": false, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.1"}]}, "turns": 2, "seconds": 6.679, "tool_calls": 1, "tool_result_chars": 147086, "input_tokens": 6, "output_tokens": 703, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 65685, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2038, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T06:56:37+00:00"}
